  "id": 203989948575041,
  "uuid": "6da28994-3c95-4dd7-bc9f-6d80ce3ed26e",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "0ba88d81-6c1b-12e9-3038-83288dc11ffa",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "265128c5-f686-799b-a785-9a9bb4612966",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In this spirit, AKU's Institute for Educational Development, East Africa (IED, EA), through its Centre for Continuing Education and Lifelong Learning (CELL), facilitated a two-day leadership workshop for AKU students in Tanzania. The workshop, themed ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "\"Leading with Purpose: Empowering Student Leaders for Partnership and Impact,\"",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " brought together more than 40 students from AKU's School of Nursing and Midwifery, Medical College, and IED, EA. The initiative was sponsored by the Student Affairs Office, Tanzania.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "At the workshop students were encouraged to rethink what leadership means in today's complex university environment. Rather than viewing it as authority or position, participants explored leadership as service, empathy, and partnership and an ongoing practice grounded in collaboration and shared purpose.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Tage Biswalo, facilitator and faculty member at IED, EA, emphasized that effective leadership begins with understanding oneself and extends to how one engages with others. Through guided reflection and dialogue, students deepened their self-awareness and emotional intelligence, learning how communication, conflict management, and interpersonal effectiveness shape meaningful leadership. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Students also had the opportunity to learn directly from AKU leadership. Professor Eunice Pallangyo, Associate Vice Provost, AKU, Tanzania and Professor Jane Rarieya, Dean, IED EA, shared insights from their leadership journeys and offered practical guidance on integrity, resilience, and the responsibility that comes with leading in a values-driven institution.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "They also explored ethical and accountable leadership and examined how innovation, collaboration, and responsible digital engagement can positively shape student governance. By the end of the workshop, students expressed a commitment to stand as partners in strengthening institutional culture and driving positive change across the university.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Reflecting on the experience, Nasoro Hamisi, a Class Representative in the undergraduate Nursing programme, noted that the workshop had been timely for his leadership role, helping him understand the ability to influence, inspire, and mobilize others towards shared goals. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Faustinah Mwabili, a student from IED EA, shared that the sessions on emotional intelligence were particularly impactful. They strengthened her ability to understand and manage her own emotions, recognize the emotions of others, and respond in ways that foster positive relationships and constructive outcomes.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "AKU continues to invest in developing student leaders who are reflective, value-driven, and equipped to lead with purpose within the University and beyond through initiatives like these.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
